{
  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "**The problem.** Given the `root` of a binary search tree with at least two nodes, return the **minimum absolute difference** between the values of any two different nodes."
    },
    {
      "type": "drawing",
      "src": "/drawings/261eb6d2-aca8-42df-b626-6674d187e9e3.svg",
      "alt": "The tree 4, 2, 6, 1, 3. Its in-order walk is 1, 2, 3, 4, 6, which is sorted. The closest pair of values must sit next to each other in that list, so only neighbours need comparing: the gaps are 1, 1, 1 and 2, and the answer is 1.",
      "width": 722,
      "height": 398,
